# Greeks and Implied Volatility Computation

Computes Black-Scholes implied volatility, delta, gamma, theta, vega, and rho for option contracts using per-contract aggregate bars. Writes **separate output files** — never modifies downloaded data.

Requires treasury yield curve data for risk-free rate interpolation.

## Prerequisites

```bash
# One-time: download US Treasury yield curve (2003–present)
python scripts/options/download_treasury_yields.py
# Output: data/treasury-yields/treasury_yields.csv
```

## Chain Greeks

Computes IV and Greeks for individual option contracts from the chain download pipeline.

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `compute_chain_greeks.py` | Single-ticker worker |
| `compute_chain_greeks_parallel_download.py` | Parallel dispatcher |
| `compute_chain_greeks_parallel_status.py` | Status monitor |

```bash
# Prerequisites: chain data must exist
python scripts/options/options_chain_discover.py --ohlcv_tickers --year 2025
python scripts/options/options_chain_parallel_download.py --ohlcv_tickers --year 2025 --spawn 50

# Compute Greeks
python scripts/options/compute_chain_greeks_parallel_download.py --ohlcv_tickers --year 2025 --spawn 16
python scripts/options/compute_chain_greeks_parallel_status.py --year 2025 --watch
```

### Input
`data/options/chains/<agg>/<year>/<ticker>_<year>_<agg>_chains.csv`

### Output (13 columns)
`data/options/chains/<agg>/<year>/<ticker>_<year>_<agg>_chains_greeks.csv`

```
ticker, timestamp, contract_symbol, strike, call_put, expiry,
days_to_expiry, implied_volatility, delta, gamma, theta, vega, rho
```

### Computation per row
- Uses `close` as option price, `underlying_price` as spot
- Skips row if close ≤ intrinsic_value (no time premium) or missing data
- Newton-Raphson IV solver (20 iterations, sigma ∈ [0.001, 5.0])
- Risk-free rate: linear interpolation of treasury yield curve by DTE

## Options Features Greeks

Computes IV and Greeks for ATM and 30-day contracts from the options features pipeline.

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `compute_stocks_greeks.py` | Single-ticker worker |
| `compute_stocks_greeks_parallel_download.py` | Parallel dispatcher |
| `compute_stocks_greeks_parallel_status.py` | Status monitor |

```bash
# Prerequisites: options features data must exist (from stock_options_from_flatfiles)
python scripts/options/compute_stocks_greeks_parallel_download.py --ohlcv_tickers --year 2025 --spawn 16
python scripts/options/compute_stocks_greeks_parallel_status.py --year 2025 --watch
```

### Input
`data/options/stocks/<agg>/<year>/<ticker>_<year>_<agg>_options.csv`

### Output (26 columns)
`data/options/stocks/<agg>/<year>/<ticker>_<year>_<agg>_options_greeks.csv`

```
ticker, timestamp,
atm_call_iv, atm_call_delta, atm_call_gamma, atm_call_theta, atm_call_vega, atm_call_rho,
atm_put_iv, atm_put_delta, atm_put_gamma, atm_put_theta, atm_put_vega, atm_put_rho,
iv30d_call_iv, iv30d_call_delta, iv30d_call_gamma, iv30d_call_theta, iv30d_call_vega, iv30d_call_rho,
iv30d_put_iv, iv30d_put_delta, iv30d_put_gamma, iv30d_put_theta, iv30d_put_vega, iv30d_put_rho
```

### Contracts computed per row
| Prefix | Price source | Strike source | DTE source | Type |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `atm_call` | `atm_call_close` | `atm_strike` | `atm_days_to_expiry` | Call |
| `atm_put` | `atm_put_close` | `atm_strike` | `atm_days_to_expiry` | Put |
| `iv30d_call` | `iv30d_call_close` | `iv30d_strike` | `iv30d_days_to_expiry` | Call |
| `iv30d_put` | `iv30d_put_close` | `iv30d_strike` | `iv30d_days_to_expiry` | Put |

## Arguments (all compute scripts)

| Argument | Required | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--tickers` | No* | — | Comma-separated symbols |
| `--tickers_file` | No* | — | CSV with `ticker` column |
| `--ohlcv_tickers` | No* | — | Derive tickers from `data/SPY/1min/<year>/` |
| `--year` | Yes | — | Year, e.g. `2025` |
| `--aggregate` | No | `1min` | `1sec`, `1min`, `5min`, `15min`, `1H`, `4H`, `1D` |
| `--output` | No | `data/` | Base output directory |
| `--resume` | No | off | Skip tickers with existing output |
| `--yields_file` | No | `data/treasury-yields/treasury_yields.csv` | Yield curve path |

*One of these ticker sources is required. Parallel scripts additionally require `--spawn N`.

## Black-Scholes implementation

- No external dependencies — uses `math.erf` and `math.exp` only (no scipy)
- Normal CDF: `0.5 * (1 + erf(x / sqrt(2)))`
- IV solver: Newton-Raphson, initial guess σ = 0.3, convergence threshold 0.0001
- Greeks: analytic partial derivatives of BS formula
- Vega and Rho scaled to 1% change (standard convention)
- Theta annualized then divided by 365 for per-day value

## Notes

- Input files are never modified — Greeks written to separate `*_greeks.csv` files
- Join with input using Pandas: `df.merge(greeks_df, on=['ticker', 'timestamp', 'contract_symbol'])`
- Chain Greeks skip rows where close ≤ intrinsic_value (deep ITM, no time premium to solve)
- Treasury yields fallback to 4.0% flat rate if file not found
